From faca32ed9a392a8255f51990cfd9e759f4103bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 17:39:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/43] test(chexc): cite section titles instead of numbers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 2026-08-20 proposal revision renumbered inference, unchecked exceptions,
conversions and adapt, invalidating every "§6.x" in the suite at a stroke.
Titles ("assumption imports", "capability capturing") survive renumbering, so
each case still says which rule it pins without the citation rotting.

74 files; runner directives (EXEC/ASSERT/DEPENDENCE) were excluded from the
rewrite by construction and verified afterwards -- 153 EXEC directives intact,
CheckedExceptions 83/83.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
